    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T0H1N28",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: second XOR stage of stage 0's partial sum (chain 8 of 13), Y = NAND(A0, T0H1N1A8.Y), feeding T0H1SUM8.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction — there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages — and each stage's carry-out, which must reach the next stage's several carry-in pins — are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_6b755ef2d5a745fda5eb1fa758d93518",
        "IdGuid": "948be6f8-c2b2-419d-843c-e1f38d88063d",
