      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T2H1N33",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: second XOR stage of stage 2's partial sum (chain 3 of 7), Y = NAND(B2, T2H1N1B3.Y), feeding T2H1SUM3.B. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction — there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages — and each stage's carry-out, which must reach the next stage's several carry-in pins — are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_8d3e28191e0646ea8ef15cd234316fae",
        "IdGuid": "bdec074c-7424-44dd-999d-0e0d3dbf41bf",
