    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "NOT1",
        "Description": "NOT reading (input A, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.375) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the load-enabled bit: select inversion, Y = NOT(Load), feeding NANDA.B — the hold arm of the multiplexer in front of the register. The fan-out of Load onto NOT1 and NANDB happens at the logic layer: both unconnected pins share the persisted signal name Load, so one network toggle drives them without a waveguide. The whole bit composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction — there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here.",
        "Identifier": "group_9206df6da56e4afba337a93529c6aab0",
        "IdGuid": "8e232aad-6d31-4fa5-9244-32a8f22b9f88",
